From: 1582130940 <19632674+1582130940@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 17:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: mediatek: make AN7581 PHY LED pinctrl optional

AN7581 boards can either route the internal PHY LED pins through the PHY
LED pinctrl state, or expose board LEDs as ordinary GPIO LEDs. Gemtek
W1700K uses GPIO LEDs for its internal switch ports and does not provide a
"gbe-led" pinctrl state on the enabled internal PHY nodes.

The AN7581 PHY probe currently unconditionally requests the "gbe-led"
state, which prints "Failed to setup PHY LED pinctrl" on boards without
that optional state even though forwarding is unaffected.

Only request the state when the PHY node actually declares pinctrl states.
Boards that declare the wrong state name still keep the error, matching the
EVB fix that renamed "led" to "gbe-led".

Signed-off-by: 1582130940 <19632674+1582130940@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/mediatek/mtk-ge-soc.c
@@ -1094,11 +1094,13 @@ static int an7581_phy_probe(struct phy_d
 	struct mtk_socphy_priv *priv;
 	struct pinctrl *pinctrl;
 
-	/* Toggle pinctrl to enable PHY LED */
-	pinctrl = devm_pinctrl_get_select(&phydev->mdio.dev, "gbe-led");
-	if (IS_ERR(pinctrl))
-		dev_err(&phydev->mdio.bus->dev,
-			"Failed to setup PHY LED pinctrl\n");
+	if (of_property_present(phydev->mdio.dev.of_node, "pinctrl-names")) {
+		/* Toggle pinctrl to enable PHY LED */
+		pinctrl = devm_pinctrl_get_select(&phydev->mdio.dev, "gbe-led");
+		if (IS_ERR(pinctrl))
+			dev_err(&phydev->mdio.bus->dev,
+				"Failed to setup PHY LED pinctrl\n");
+	}
 
 	priv = devm_kzalloc(&phydev->mdio.dev, sizeof(*priv), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!priv)
